{"affected":[{"defaultStatus":"unaffected","original_ranges":[{"lessThanOrEqual":"22.23.3","status":"affected","version":"22.23.3","versionType":"semver"},{"lessThanOrEqual":"24.22.0","status":"affected","version":"24.22.0","versionType":"semver"},{"lessThanOrEqual":"26.12.0","status":"affected","version":"26.12.0","versionType":"semver"}],"product":"node","vendor":"nodejs"}],"aliases":["CVE-2026-106074"],"assertions":[{"affected_indices":[0],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"A flaw in Node.js `crypto` causes the internal entropy caches used by `crypto.randomUUID()`, `crypto.randomUUIDv7()`, and `crypto.randomInt()` to be saved into user-land startup snapshots (`--build-snapshot`) and single executable applications built with `useSnapshot`.\n\nIf any of these functions, or an API that relies on them such as `URL.createObjectURL()`, is called while the snapshot is built, every process started from that snapshot returns the same values until the cache is refilled: up to 127 UUIDs and about 1,000 `randomInt()` values. Identifiers expected to be unique can collide across processes, and values issued by one process can be predicted by observing another.\n\nThis vulnerability affects Node.js **26.x**, **24.x**, and **22.x**."}],"metrics":[{"cvssV3_0":{"baseScore":4.8,"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","vectorString":"CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N","version":"3.0"}}],"problemTypes":[{"descriptions":[{"cweId":"CWE-330","description":"CWE-330 Use of Insufficiently Random Values","lang":"en","type":"CWE"}]}],"provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-10-23T16:15:05.829Z","orgId":"36234546-b8fa-4601-9d6f-f4e334aa8ea1","shortName":"hackerone"},"role":"cna"},{"affected_indices":[],"metrics":[{"other":{"content":{"id":"CVE-2026-106074","options":[{"Exploitation":"none"},{"Automatable":"no"},{"Technical Impact":"partial"}],"role":"CISA Coordinator","timestamp":"2026-11-02T15:43:34.777507Z","version":"2.0.3"},"type":"ssvc"}}],"provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-11-02T15:48:44.599Z","orgId